### Try the student flow by hand. Start the app first: ./mvnw spring-boot:run
### IntelliJ, or VS Code with the "REST Client" extension: click "Send Request" on each block, top to bottom.
### Data is in memory: restarting the app clears it and ids start again at 1.

### 1. Upload a file from the computer (notes.txt is next to this file)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/materials
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="notes.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

< ./notes.txt
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="userId"

1
--boundary--

### 2. ...or paste text instead
POST http://localhost:8080/api/materials/text
Content-Type: application/json

{"userId": 1, "title": "Water cycle", "content": "Water evaporates from oceans when the sun heats it. The vapour cools and condenses into clouds, then falls as rain."}

### 3. My materials
GET http://localhost:8080/api/materials?userId=1

### 4. Generate a test from material 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/exams
Content-Type: application/json

{"userId": 1, "sourceMaterialIds": [1], "questionCount": 3}

### 5. My tests
GET http://localhost:8080/api/exams?userId=1

### 6. Start test 1 (copy questionIds from the response)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/exams/1/attempts?userId=1

### 7. Answer question 1, with an explanation (at least 15 words)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/attempts/1/answers
Content-Type: application/json

{"questionId": 1, "answer": "True", "explanation": "Chlorophyll in the leaves absorbs sunlight, and that light energy is what powers photosynthesis in the plant."}

### 8. Answer question 2
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/attempts/1/answers
Content-Type: application/json

{"questionId": 2, "answer": "True", "explanation": "The oxygen comes from water molecules that are split apart, and the plant releases it into the air."}

### 9. Submit: grades the answers and explanations
POST http://localhost:8080/api/attempts/1/submit

### 10. See the feedback again later
GET http://localhost:8080/api/attempts/1/result

### 11. My history
GET http://localhost:8080/api/attempts?userId=1
